# File drop

Drag a file onto the zone and its name, size and type appear immediately.

## Note

This page stops at the drop half of "drop, then upload": it detects the drop
and reads the file's name, size and type. The upload half is blocked on the
file's content. `Upload body to url as T, then action.` sends `body` as the text
of one `multipart/form-data` part, and a dropped `File` carries its content in
`bytes`, which a compiled page cannot yet read as usable data
(`docs/frontend.md`'s Triggers section) — so no documented sentence turns a
drop into an upload of the file itself, and `Upload file's name to …` would send
the dropped file's name, not the file.

The handler declares `(file: File)` and binds the whole record: `file's name`,
`file's size` (its content's length, in bytes) and `file's type` (its MIME
type). Each test drives its drop with the sentence `docs/frontend.md` gives for
one, declaring the whole file:
`Raise "filedropped" on "#zone" with a new File with name … and type … and bytes [ … ].`

## Page /

State:
    Let dropCount be 0.
    Let lastName be "".
    Let lastSize be 0.
    Let lastType be "".

Actions:
    When a file is dropped on "#zone" (file: File):
        Set dropCount to dropCount + 1.
        Set lastName to file's name.
        Set lastSize to file's size.
        Set lastType to file's type.

View:
    <main class="card">
      <h1>Drop a file</h1>
      <div id="zone" class="dropzone">Drop a file here</div>
      <p id="count">{dropCount} file(s) dropped</p>
      {if dropCount is greater than 0:}
        <dl id="last">
          <dt>Name</dt><dd id="name">{lastName}</dd>
          <dt>Size</dt><dd id="size">{lastSize | plural "byte" "bytes"}</dd>
          <dt>Type</dt><dd id="type">{lastType}</dd>
        </dl>
      {end}
    </main>

Style:
    .dropzone { border: 2px dashed var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 3rem; text-align: center; color: var(--muted); }

## Test: the zone starts empty

Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "0 file(s) dropped".
Expect that "#last" is hidden.

## Test: dropping a file shows its name, size and type, and counts it

Raise "filedropped" on "#zone" with a new File with name "receipt.pdf" and type "application/pdf" and bytes [37, 80, 68, 70, 45].
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "1 file(s) dropped".
Expect that the text of "#name" is equal to "receipt.pdf".
Expect that the text of "#size" is equal to "5 bytes".
Expect that the text of "#type" is equal to "application/pdf".

## Test: a second drop replaces the details and keeps counting

Raise "filedropped" on "#zone" with a new File with name "receipt.pdf" and type "application/pdf" and bytes [37, 80, 68, 70, 45].
Raise "filedropped" on "#zone" with a new File with name "photo.png" and type "image/png" and bytes [137, 80, 78, 71].
Expect that the text of "#count" is equal to "2 file(s) dropped".
Expect that the text of "#name" is equal to "photo.png".
Expect that the text of "#size" is equal to "4 bytes".
Expect that the text of "#type" is equal to "image/png".
